  "summary": "The Yakima City Council voted 5-1 to renew a roughly $250,000 annual contract with Flock Safety covering 87 fixed license plate readers, after an initial 3-3 vote failed and was reconsidered. The renewal came despite community concerns about privacy, ARPA funding use, Flock's terms of service, and compliance with Washington's SB 6002; Police Chief Boyle said three cameras were removed to comply with the new law.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Yakima City Council members voted to renew a contract with Flock Safety in a last-minute reversal on Tuesday night.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Yakima Police Chief Shawn Boyle said the department evaluated its camera locations after the law passed and removed three of its 87 fixed cameras to comply with the law.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Data in Washington state is permanently deleted after 21 days.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "In the second vote, only Gonzalez voted against the renewal.",
      "paragraph_idx": 22
    }
  ],
